From: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] docker daemon.json: max-download-attempts 25 (Odoo #2136)

dockerd gives one layer 5 connections and then fails the pull. Every connection
that ends early is resumed, but it counts. On a slow link that cut each
connection after 20 MiB a 375 MiB layer needed 19 and could never finish.
25 covers that layer with 30 % margin (25 x 20 MiB = 500 MiB per layer; the
largest layer of GA Core 2026.10.4.6 armv7 is 243 MiB = 13 connections).

Read by the graph-driver (overlay2) image service only. With the containerd
snapshotter (the default of a freshly flashed data partition) dockerd does not
use the key; containerd reconnects without an attempt budget while it makes
progress. tests/gates/docker_daemon_json pins the value.
---
 buildroot-external/rootfs-overlay/etc/docker/daemon.json | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/buildroot-external/rootfs-overlay/etc/docker/daemon.json b/buildroot-external/rootfs-overlay/etc/docker/daemon.json
--- a/buildroot-external/rootfs-overlay/etc/docker/daemon.json
+++ b/buildroot-external/rootfs-overlay/etc/docker/daemon.json
@@ -5,5 +5,6 @@
     },
     "data-root": "/mnt/data/docker",
     "bip": "172.30.232.1/23",
-    "ipv6": true
+    "ipv6": true,
+    "max-download-attempts": 25
 }
